## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design cost-aware, privacy-conscious edge ML with real-world trade-offs for a safety-critical feature.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML constraints and quantization
- Real-time latency vs accuracy
- Privacy, data minimization, and compliance
- Telemetry strategy and cloud-feedback loops
- Rollout, monitoring, and break-even metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo on-device scoring stub
function scoreManeuver(telemetry) {
  // telemetry: {acc, gps, speed, time}
  // returns anomaly score 0-1
  return sigmoid(model.predict(telemetry));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle model drift without frequent cloud updates?
- What would be your go/no-go criteria for a first production release?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to translate product goals into a concrete cost model that accounts for on-device constraints, security requirements, and regulatory concerns. It also probes understanding of trade-offs for multi-app isolation, update mechanics, and privacy-by-design principles.

## Key Concepts
- On-device ML model footprints and TEE (Trusted Execution Environment) architecture
- Cross-app isolation with per-app policy overrides
- Telemetry budgeting and data minimization under privacy regulations
- OTA update economics, delta patching, and cryptographic key rotation
- Compliance frameworks (GDPR, CCPA), privacy-by-design, and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-break-even calculator
function needsGoNoGo(serverSavingsPerMonth, deviceCostsPerMonth, months) {
  const netSavings = serverSavingsPerMonth - deviceCostsPerMonth;
  const cumulativeSavings = netSavings * months;
  return {
    breakEvenMonths: deviceCostsPerMonth / netSavings,
    go: cumulativeSavings > 0 && months >= 18
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests candidate ability to design a mixed on-device/offload chat triage, evaluating lifecycle costs and business impact of privacy-preserving UX.

## Key Concepts

- On-device NLP model size and latency
- Cloud handoff economics
- Local storage and OTA updates
- Compliance and user trust
- Rollout and measurement plan

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code for on-device classifier trigger
function triage(input) {
  const intent = onDeviceModel.predict(input);
  if (isComplex(intent)) {
    return cloudHandoff(input);
  }
  return generateResponse(intent);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure incremental savings from reduced cloud fetches?
- What telemetry would you collect to monitor quality without compromising privacy?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about client-side privacy, offline UX, and cost trade-offs without server trust. The candidate must specify concrete numbers, crypto choices, and go/no-go criteria, balancing performance, storage, and regulatory costs.

## Key Concepts

- Client-side encryption and key management
- Data growth and local cache sizing
- Delta synchronization vs full sync
- Privacy/compliance implications and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example using Web Crypto API AES-GCM
async function encrypt(plaintext, cryptoKey) {
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const encrypted = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(
    { name: 'AES-GCM', iv },
    cryptoKey,
    new TextEncoder().encode(plaintext)
  );
  return { encrypted, iv };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Explores cost trade-offs of on-device privacy-preserving telemetry at scale, balancing data minimization with operational transparency.

## Key Concepts

- On-device aggregation and secure aggregation
- Data minimization vs. data utility
- Compliance costs vs. backend savings
- Phased rollout and break-even metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: merge deltas with secure aggregation placeholder
function aggregateDeltas(deltas, state) {
  // secure-aggregate-friendly merge
  const merged = deltas.reduce((acc, d) => acc + d.value, 0);
  state.total += merged;
  return state;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you model drift and re-authorization costs if consent preferences change?
- What latency/throughput targets would you set for real-time dashboards under offline conditions?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses cost-aware design of privacy-preserving observability with edge processing, cross-region deployment, and go/no-go decisions.

## Key Concepts
- Edge compute budgeting
- Privacy-first telemetry
- Data retention and regional regulations
- Multi-region cost models
- Rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function cba(params) {
  // simple cost model
  const deviceCost = params.deviceCPU * 0.1 + params.deviceMem * 0.05;
  const deltaCost = (params.deltaKB / 1024) * 0.02;
  const centralCost = params.retentionMonths * 1000 * 0.01;
  return deviceCost + deltaCost + centralCost;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for GDPR/CCPA across regions?
- What metrics would tie cost to business value beyond raw savings?

## Why This Is Asked

Gauges ability to justify product bets with a pragmatic, numbers-driven approach and to handle uncertainty in inputs.

## Key Concepts

- Cost estimation
- Benefit estimation
- Break-even analysis
- Reasonable assumptions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple CBA calculator
function cba(params) {
  const {maU, lift, arpu, months, cost} = params;
  const annualizedBenefit = maU * lift * arpu * months;
  return {annualizedBenefit, cost, breakevenMonths: cost / (annualizedBenefit || 1)};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust if MAU grows or adoption changes?
- What if ARPU uplift is not uniform across user segments?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to translate connectivity challenges into a minimal, privacy-conscious on-device flow with cost trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Edge batching, offline queues, deduping
- Energy/memory budgeting, latency impact
- Privacy, consent, rollout strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
function batchRequests(requests, maxBatch) {
  const batches = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < requests.length; i += maxBatch) {
    batches.push(requests.slice(i, i + maxBatch));
  }
  return batches;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle failed batches in poor connectivity differently for iOS vs Android?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate break-even without compromising privacy?
